{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 1, :comments ["<b>And Joseph was brought down to Egypt.</b> Our Rabbis of blessed memory interpreted: the son of a maidservant sells the son of a free woman, and a slave buys him. For the Midianites sold him — they being descendants of the maidservant, descendants of Hagar — and Potiphar was a slave, and the verse was fulfilled (Ecclesiastes 10): ״ראיתי עבדים על סוסים״. And the officer of the executioners — this was the one appointed to kill all those liable to execution by decree of the king, and he was a mighty warrior and possessed of might, like Nebuzaradan who was a great officer, in the manner of what is written (Jeremiah 39): ״וישלח נבוזראדן רב טבחים״, and it is written (II Kings 25): ״ואת יתר ההמון הגלה נבוזראדן רב טבחים״. And likewise we find regarding Arioch it is written (Daniel 2): ״באדין דניאל התיב עיטה וטעם לאריוך רב טבחיא די מלכא״." "<b>By way of the Midrash.</b> ״ויוסף הורד מצרימה״ — There is an account of King Antoninus who came to his Caesarea and sent for our holy Rabbi. Our holy Rabbi came, and Rabbi Shimon his son was with him, and Rabbi Ḥiyya the Elder. Rabbi Shimon saw there a fine and praiseworthy legion, its head reaching the Capitol of columns. Rabbi Shimon said to Rabbi Ḥiyya: See how many fattened calves of Esau! Rabbi Ḥiyya took him and led him to the market and showed him a basket of figs and a basket of grapes with flies upon them. Rabbi Ḥiyya said: These flies and that legion you saw — which of them is more praiseworthy? When Rabbi Shimon went up to his father, he said to him: Thus I said to Rabbi Ḥiyya, and thus he answered me. His father said to him: Until now the Babylonian gave him substance, for he compared them to flies — because these legions are accounted as nothing, but flies — the Holy One, blessed be He, carries out His mission through them, as is said (Isaiah 7:18): ״והיה ביום ההוא ישרק ה׳ לזבוב אשר בקצה יארי מצרים ולדבורה אשר בארץ אשור״. And likewise it is written (Exodus 23): ״ושלחתי את הצרעה לפניך״. And likewise with lice and frogs. Know that when the Holy One, blessed be He, wished to fulfill a known decree, know that He carried out His mission through the youngest of the tribes: Joseph was sold to Egypt, and his father and his brothers went down there and paid the note. Therefore it says: ״ויוסף הורד מצרימה״."], :book :genesis, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 39, :notes {0 "Source citations normalized: קהלת י → Ecclesiastes 10; ירמיה לט → Jeremiah 39; מ\"ב כה → II Kings 25; דניאל ב → Daniel 2.", 1 "Citation ישעיה ז יח normalized to Isaiah 7:18; שמות כג to Exodus 23. The heading ובמדרש rendered as the fixed method-header 'By way of the Midrash.'"}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:18:51.271790387Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}